COMM4353.description:
Strategic Management focuses on how a firm competes at various levels (functional, business, corporate, and international). The course is designed to analyze the sources of competitive advantage among firms and to develop knowledge and skills necessary for effectively analyzing, formulating, and implementing strategy. 

By the end of the course, the student should: 

1.  Understand the key concepts, tools and techniques in competitive strategy, strategy formulation, and strategy implementation; 

2.  Understand relevant methods and decision criteria in making strategic decisions; 

3.  Have an ability to use the appropriate concepts, tools, and techniques when discerning key issues, analyzing situations, and making sound decisions in a variety of strategic situations; and

4.  Have oral and written communication skills that enable the effective presentation of strategic management and implementation concepts within the case-study format.

TYPR1000.description:
Students will complete a pre-departure online course titled Global Competency Development, over a 3-week period. They will visit Colombia for two weeks, where they will attend daily classes, as well as participate in sociocultural activities and excursions organized in collaboration with the Universidad Catolica de Manizales. 

As well as studying the language, culture and politics of Colombia, students will visit social projects and historical sites. Specific details of the course description will vary according to the destination if the Field Course is held in other locations in future years.

Objectives:
1. develop cultural awareness and challenge cultural biases and stereotypes;
2. facilitate and collaborate respectfully in multicultural communities;
3. exercise perspective-taking at interpersonal, local, and global level;
4. identify and capitalize on one's potential contributions in the immediate environment;
5. understand that developing global competencies is a life-long process;
6. develop basic Spanish language skills;
7. understand the Colombian socio-political context;
8. develop democracy and peace-building skills.
